course-assets/scenes/module-17/_logs/m17_L17_b09_slip-vs-pocket.png.log:15:Generate one image with gpt-image-2 and save it to course-assets/scenes/module-17/m17_L17_b09_slip-vs-pocket.png (PNG, 1600x900). Match the attached style references and cast-board character style exactly. COMPOSITION: A split composition divided by a simple vertical black line. LEFT half: a rounded rectangular card lying flat and tilted, drawn in pale cream with a drooping wilted look, slightly faded. RIGHT half: an upright bright yellow rounded card with a clean black check mark, and just below it a doodle trouser pocket with MONEY-GREEN bank-note bills (blank green notes, no writing) tucked into it. Conveys: neglected work fades, thorough work becomes money in your pocket. No people. Clean blue space at the top on both halves for overlaid code text. STYLE: flat sticker-sheet doodle illustration, thick black hand-drawn outlines with a slight wobble, rounded corners, flat fills — palette is yellow, orange, cream, white, black on cornflower-blue #62b3f3, PLUS money-green used ONLY for cash / bank-notes (an intentional communication exception so money reads as money). No gradients, no texture, no shadows, no lighting, no perspective, no skin-tone shading. Faces use flat white/cream fill, tiny dot eyes, small subtle curved cast-board nose, simple mouth. Cylindrical limbs, strong simple silhouettes, confidently imperfect hand-drawn. No ambient doodles: no hearts, sparkles, notes, thought bubbles, motion marks, icons, random props, or decorative clutter. No text, letters, words, numbers, symbols, dollar signs, labels, captions, screens with writing, or readable paperwork anywhere. Leave clean open cornflower-blue space for code-rendered Sticker overlays. 16:9 composition, 1600x900 PNG.
