docs/course-production/scripts/gen_stills_8A.sh:41:  gen "m08_L8A_b03_underwater.png" "$A/marcus.png" "$MARCUS" "EXACTLY ONE person: MARCUS AND the simple doodle house beside him are BOTH standing in flood water — this is ONE single continuous body of water with ONE flat water surface, so the SAME horizontal wavy WATER line crosses BOTH Marcus's body AND the house at the SAME height in the image. That one wavy line sits at upper-window height on the house (near the top of the house body, just below the roofline) and crosses MARCUS at his neck/shoulders (since he is standing right beside the house, his much shorter body is submerged nearly up to his neck by that same water level). Everything below that single line — most of Marcus's body, the house's upper window, door, and lower window — is submerged and tinted muted underwater-blue. Only Marcus's head/shoulders and the house's roof, chimney, and gutter line stay above the water in normal palette colors. THERE IS ONLY ONE WAVY LINE IN THE ENTIRE IMAGE, and it is perfectly level/horizontal all the way across, passing through both Marcus and the house at the same height — no second wave line, no ripples, no other wavy marks anywhere. Marcus's worried face and one hand on his head are visible above the water; his expression is worried, looking at the house. Centered composition, generous open cornflower-blue space around. EXACTLY ONE PERSON." ;;
